cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this compiler in your research or teaching materials, please cite it as below."
title: "Cambridge IGCSE & A Level Pseudocode Compiler: a browser-based interpreter, practice and exam platform for Cambridge pseudocode"
type: software
version: 0.1.0
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.24288539
date-released: 2026-11-16
abstract: >-
  A browser-based interpreter for the pseudocode of Cambridge IGCSE Computer
  Science (0478/0984/2210) and Cambridge International AS & A Level Computer
  Science (9618). One superset ANTLR4 grammar covers both syllabuses, and an
  async tree-walking interpreter runs entirely client-side with student-friendly
  parse and runtime error messages. Around it sit autograded practice
  questions, timed exam simulation, a flowchart builder that converts drawings
  to runnable pseudocode, a sequenced Paper 2 course, and teacher classes with
  assignments and progress tracking.
